            <div xml:id="d1035">

                <pb facs="0778" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123B641/23.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brownsville, Texas</hi>]</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have you received my May 4, in which I earnestly recommended that the diplomatic
                    representatives of various friendly nations be requested to take action and
                    prompt measures to bring about the release from prison of Vice Consul Silliman
                    at Saltillo, also Consul Bonney at San Luis Potosi, and take them and their
                    American colonies out of federal territory. Both Consuls are understood to still
                    be in prison; also several American citizens. There is no possible connection
                    between Monterey and Saltillo nor San Luis Potosi, but the railroad is open
                    south of these cities to Mexico City. Vice Consul Silliman was a classmate in
                    Princeton College with President Wilson, graduating from same class. I feel sure
                    that friendly diplomats can obtain their release. Please promptly telegraph
                    acknowledgement of receipt of this telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
